{
  "title": "Idiopathic Chondromalacia Patellae",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3022/idiopathic-chondromalacia-patellae",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 31 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Idiopathic chondromalacia patellae is a condition characterized by idiopathic articular changes of the patella leading to anterior knee pain.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is clinical with a history of anterior knee pain made worse with squatting, prolonged sitting or ascending stairs and pain on patellar compression in knee extension.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally nonoperative with resting, ice, activity modifications and physical therapy to focus on hamstring, quadriceps and core strengthening.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common occurs in adolescents and young adults",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "women > men",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain generator is not clearly understood and multi-factorial",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may result from roughening or damage to the undersurface cartilage of the patella",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "numerous factors have been proposed including",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "limb malaligment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "muscle weakness",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "chondral lesions",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "patella maltracking",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "patella maltracking can create narrow contact pressure points and further attenuate pain.",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "elevated contact pressures between patella and femoral groove are associated with anterior knee pain",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**miserable malalignment syndrome**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "a term coined for anatomic characteristics that lead to an increased Q angle and an exacerbation of patellofemoral dysplasia. They include",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "femoral anteversion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "genu valgum",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "external tibial torsion / pronated feet",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Patellofemoral joint",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "articulation between patella and intracondylar groove of femur",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pain receptors of the knee",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "subchondral bone has weak potential to generate pain signals",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "anterior fat pad and joint capsule have **highest potential** for pain signals",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
